gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.time=Time per Batch\nComplete time to process one ore. Hover for mechanics; click ▶ for the step-by-step derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.parallel=Parallel\nOres processed per batch. Click ▶ for the derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.thru=Throughput\nTheoretical processing speed. Click ▶ for the derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.formula=Actual weighted formula\nTime-weighted steam composition of the current chain (general formula in the chain steam ▶ derivation).
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.fmod=Per-segment summary\nOne overview line per logistics module.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.heat=Heat\nPreheat progress 0~100%; a batch can only start at full heat.\nHeats up in 30 s; steam loss -0.5%/s, idle -1%/s.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.lube=Lubricant\nTwo segments combined, per-second basis. Click ▶ for the derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.thru_real=Real-time throughput\nOres actually completed in the last 1-second window.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.total=Total processed\nTotal ores that entered the cluster since it started.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.steam_total=Total steam (weighted all-chain)\nΣ executable-chain steam × multiplier × (1-saver), fixed terms excluded.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.steam_chain=Chain steam (formula-weighted)\nTheoretical steam power of the selected unit's chain.\nClick ▶ for the full step-by-step derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.steam_settle=Steam (settled)\nActual deduction per second. Click ▶ for the derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.lube_split=Lubricant segments\nMechanics under Runtime Summary "Lubricant". Click ▶ for the breakdown.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost.0=Nitric acid (parallel booster)\nEffect: +8 ores per batch.\nConsumption per unit: deducted once per batch by the actual ore count.\nClick ▶ for the unit-price and per-batch derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost.1=Hydrochloric acid (speed booster)\nEffect: working-segment time ÷(1+speed total).\nNot installed; once installed the unit price = base table ÷ 10 — click ▶ for the four-tier price table.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost.2=Sulfuric acid (primary-output booster)\nSame kind takes the max with only one active; single peak: the peak step is full, other processing steps ×0.1.\nUnit price = base table ÷ 10 (bronze 80 → 8 L/ore), deducted by actual ore count per batch.\nNo steam multiplier.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost.3=Ammonium chloride (secondary-output booster)\nSecondary-output chance stacks additively, can exceed 100%; crush steps weakened by cluster tier ×0.1/×0.5/none.\nUnit price = base table ÷ 10 (bronze 20 → 2 L/ore).\nNo steam multiplier.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost.4=Coolant (steam-saver booster)\nSteam saving: weighted all-chain ×(1-saver rate), additive capped at 48%; fixed terms and lubricant unaffected.\nUnit price = base table ÷ 10 (bronze 10 → 1 L/ore).\nNo steam multiplier.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.chains_count=Chains\nNumber of logistics chains identified; a chain = one logistics unit's processing order.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.chains_steps=Total steps / longest / avg length\nA chain step = one processing operation on the chain.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.boost_state=Active / failed\nCannot afford a full batch → failed for this batch: bonus and multiplier removed, the batch continues.\nOn failure a chat notice is sent once (latched, not repeated before the next successful run); terminal and logistics modules stay in sync.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_speed=Speed booster total\nΣ of speed modules.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_parallel=Parallel booster total\nΣ of parallel modules, added to the logistics base.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_primary=Primary-output booster\nSame kind takes the max.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_secondary=Secondary-output booster\nAdditive stack Σ.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_saver=Steam-saver rate\nAdditive stack Σ, capped at 48%.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.sum_mult=Steam multiplier\nSpeed/parallel modules multiplied per unit by tier. Click ▶ for the derivation.
gtsr.terminal.perf.tip.cost=Booster cost (per-batch basis)\nDeducted once per batch, scaling with batch size. Click ▶ for the derivation.
