gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.secondary.value=Secondary bonus: +%s by tier
gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.steam_saver.desc=Steam saver booster: cuts running steam; stacks across modules; more same-kind modules raise booster fluid cost (10% synergy each); steam penalty scales only with structure tier
gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.steam_saver.value=Steam saving: %s by tier, cap %s
gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.logistics.desc=Logistics unit: cluster chain executor with four I/O types (normal or ME hatches accepted)
gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.logistics.soft_hammer=Soft hammer toggle (powered on by default)
gtsr.tooltip.cluster.unit.logistics.queue=Queue mode: screwdriver toggles; when enabled a batch starts only after a single item type reaches the parallel count


# BQ quests BEGIN
### Quest Lines ###

## GT Steam Reborn

betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Steam Reborn
betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=A full steam-age expansion for GregTech: 23 steam multiblocks, the singularity tech chain, and a cross-dimensional hub-and-node logistics network.%n%nSix chapters: steam economics, three wells of steam, the processing matrix, hub logistics, the singularity depths, and Reborn in Electricity.%n%nSteam is all you need.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§2§lSteam Reborn
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=Welcome to Steam Reborn. GregTech's steam age gets reinvented here: §623 steam multiblocks§r, §da singularity tech chain§r and a cross-dimensional hub logistics network.%n%nThe line moves in chapters: §6steam economics§r, §6three wells of steam§r, §3the processing matrix§r, §5hub logistics§r, then down into the §ddeepest current layer of singularities§r, with a look at §3Reborn in Electricity§r.%n%nEvery machine runs on two tracks: a mechanics lesson first, then a hands-on acceptance of the controller.%n%n§8§oZero EU spent, from one boiler all the way to the singularity's doorstep.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§6§lSteam Economics
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=This lesson skips the machines and covers GTSR's under-the-hood mixin tweaks — no new blocks, just quality-of-life.%n%nSneak right-click a boiler controller with an empty hand to §2decalc it on the spot§r; a screwdriver gives input hatches and input busses §6auto-input§r (fed from the inventory in front) and toggles their filters; steam input busses accept direct pipe extraction, steam output busses learned auto-output; GT5U's own steam multiblocks now take cooling hatches; and the redstone hatch fits any multiblock (up to four per machine), emitting a signal that tracks progress.%n%n§8§oNot a single new machine — yet you will meet them everywhere.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§6§lA Tide of Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=Boilers are only the start — this mod both makes and spends enormous amounts of steam: the §6Large Geothermal Steam Boiler§r burns magma around the clock; the §6Large Solar Overpressure Array§r moves the boiler room into the sky and lives on the weather; and the §6Gear Steam Compressor§r — note, it does not make steam — takes plain steam, pays a cost, and yields theoretically less superheated.%n%nEach well has a temperament: geothermal wants magma plumbing, solar runs full by day and zero by night, the compressor is an on-demand stopgap.%n%nFrom this chapter on, steam ledgers count in thousands of liters, and reservoirs are planned like seas.%n%n§3Sun by day, magma by night, compressor whenever superheated runs short.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§6§lSuperheated Means 4x
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=Superheated steam is not “better steam” — it is another tempo: the machine draws §14x steam§r per tick while recipe duration goes §1÷4§r, a net §1four-fold speedup§r.%n%nThe comforting part: total steam per recipe §2stays unchanged§r; only the pacing of throughput moves, so your capacity planning survives.%n%nBronze included, no tier gate — the earlier you switch, the earlier you enjoy it.%n%n§3Want throughput? Make superheated first.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§6§lThe Rock Breaker's Free Lunch
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=The rock breaker's recipes need glowstone dust as the spark — and the spark used to get eaten, with a circuit-6 toll on top. GTSR rewrites the rule: glowstone dust in rock breaker recipes is never consumed — the circuit-6 toll still applies, but one glowstone dust now lasts forever.%n%nBulk stone processing turns into a free lunch: the stone keeps rolling out, and not a single reagent is charged.%n%n§8§oFree reagents, endless rocks.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§6§lNext Door Shares the Boost
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=GTSR's enhancements don't stop at its own doorstep: GTNL's steam machines can share them too. Thanks to @Pseudo and runtime detection, it makes no difference whether GTNL is installed; flip gtnlEnhancement in the config and GTNL steam machines gain the same treatment — superheated steam at four times the burn for four times the speed, cooling hatches welcome.%n%nIt is off by default — and while it is off, everything stays perfectly quiet.%n%n§8§oGood things kept secret? One config toggle away.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§6§lAuto-Input at a Glance
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=Input hatches and input busses have learned to help themselves: a screwdriver's normal right-click orthogonal-cycles through the four states of input filter × auto-input, while a bus's Shift right-click keeps the original modes — just the old sort-and-limit pair.%n%nTwo speeds on the dial: fluid hatches pull 1,000 mB every 5 seconds, item busses move 1 stack every 5 seconds — all fed from the container right in front.%n%n§8§oThe machines reach out for themselves; you just manage.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§6§lGeothermal: Burn the Magma
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=The Large Geothermal Steam Boiler is the most direct idea of all: burn magma as fuel — magma is its coal bunker.%n%nPlumb in magma and a steady water source and it steams around the clock; slot a §3Geothermal Overheat Chip§r (steel and up) into the controller to switch to superheated output, with bonus minerals rolling in on the side.%n%n§8§oBurn the planet's core, mine the planet's purse.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§6§lThe Four-to-One Gate
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=Need superheated but geothermal and solar are not ready? The §3Gear Steam Compressor§r is the stopgap: it swallows plain steam, pays a cost, and yields theoretically less superheated — more in, less out, buying a steam grade off the books.%n%nIt is an emergency gate, not a mass-production answer: small gaps and impatient moments, flip it on; for serious superheated volume, the three wells themselves must deliver.%n%nStructure as always: casing, pipe, gearbox and frame in one tier.%n%n§3Superheated is nice — do not drink it like water.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§6§lSteam from the Sun
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=The §6Large Solar Overpressure Array§r moves the boiler room into the sky: no fuel, just weather — the stronger the sun, the harder it steams, and the nickel tier emits superheated outright.%n%nIt has the same §6overpressure§r mechanic: push heat up and output climbs; shade one block on top and the sunlight ratio drops accordingly. The controller slot also takes §3solar boilers§r as boosters — the four from the reward slot straight in.%n%nKeep a reservoir: at night and in the rain, the sun clocks out.%n%n§cSunlight is free, but it keeps office hours.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§3§lThe Bronze Matrix
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=Chapter C opens its seven-piece set: §3the Large Steam Furnace, Air Compressor, Atmospheric Centrifuge, Steam Fluid Drill, Vein Steam Pyrolyzer, the three kiln brothers and the Siemens-Martin§r — with the borer and chip sidelines standing by.%n%nMany machines, one accountant: every drop of steam still bills through chapter A's master formula, priced in §6L/s§r with the efficiency denominator keeping the books.%n%nSame rhythm as ever: mechanics lesson first, acceptance second.%n%n§3The more machines you run, the better you must count.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§6§lThe Cooling Ledger
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=Where does spent steam go? Plain steam condenses into §6distilled water§r and lands in the Steam Cooling Hatch; superheated steam first degrades back into plain steam and lands in the Pressure Steam Cooling Hatch.%n%nA machine without a cooling hatch runs no tab — whatever is not caught §cis simply gone§r, not a drop left.%n%nSo this ledger has exactly one key move: fit the hatch, then pipe the distilled water back to the boiler, and scale never calls again.%n%n§2Distilled water back to the boiler, no more scale headaches.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§6§lScale and Overpressure
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=Run the geothermal long enough and it §6scales up§r: the thicker the scale, the thinner the steam — neglect it and the well nearly stops. The fix is easy: sneak right-click the controller with an empty hand and scrape it clean on the spot.%n%nThere is also an §6overpressure§r trick: push heat past the red line and output climbs hard — double, if you dare. Just make sure the water supply keeps up before playing with fire.%n%n§cScale is a time tax; come scrape often.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lCompressor Online
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=Acceptance: the §3Gear Steam Compressor§r controller is the proof.%n%nThe positioning, once more: it is a stopgap thing that makes superheated steam — flip it on for small gaps, and the books will always show more in than out.%n%nIt cares nothing for weather or geology; hook it to the steam main and it works. The day the three wells cover your superheated, it can retire with honor.%n%n§2Keep the gate handy, and superheated never panics.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§6§lRoll Out the Solar Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=Acceptance: the Large Solar Overpressure Array controller is the proof.%n%nThree tiers — bronze, steel, nickel — rise with the multiblock's size, and the nickel tier emits superheated outright; casing, pipe, gearbox and frame must all match the tier to form.%n%nThe booster and heat-gain arithmetic was done in the mechanics lesson — roll out the array and let the sun do the billing.%n%n§2A boiler room in the sky, with the sun as its fuel depot.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§6§lThe Matrix Midway Gate
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=This is the matrix's midway gate: the furnace, air compressor, centrifuge, drills, kilns and Siemens-Martin stand in formation — pause here, audit the steam ledgers and main headroom, then push on.%n%nAhead, two reservoirs are already within sight; the next level, hub logistics, will weave the whole base's steam and water into one net.%n%n§6Look back from the halfway mark and see how deep the bronze reserves run — every gate ahead is affordable.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.name=§3§lThe Big Steam Furnace
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.desc=The Large Steam Furnace is the bronze base's smelting workhorse — one machine for a whole row of single furnaces: the old EU bill is re-priced in steam, and there are only two levers, §1parallelism§r and §1discounts§r, with higher tiers discounting harder.%n%nExact rates live in the tooltip; here you learn to read the levers — parallelism sets how much a batch takes in, the discount sets how thirsty each bite is, and the product is your true throughput.%n%n§cThe sky-high number in old manuals was an accident of reading per-tick as per-second — let it go.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.name=§3§lWhere Air Comes From
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.desc=Air does not come from nowhere: the Air Compressor checks no recipes and just keeps the beat — trading steam for air, pumping the network one stroke at a time, blunt and honest.%n%nIt carries its own safety net: when tank pressure runs short it falls back to the lower air tier automatically — §3the line never stalls§r. Bigger tanks mean steadier buffering; parallel for speed, pace for thrift — the numbers live in the tooltip.%n%n§8§oThe wind is free; the pump is not.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§3§lCentrifuge the Sky
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=The Atmospheric Centrifuge takes air apart into its components — the gateway of the whole chemical chain.%n%nThe Rare Gas Separation Chip is a §3recipe-table switch§r, not an accelerator: steel-only, no speed and no extra yield, and once fitted only §1rare recipes§r run while the common ones lock out.%n%nA chip is not a master key — fitted to the wrong tier it is pure waste.%n%n§cA chip on a bronze unit does nothing. Don't waste it.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§6§lFit the Cooling Hatches
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=Hardware time for last lesson's ledger: craft a §3Steam Cooling Hatch§r and a §3Pressure Steam Cooling Hatch§r, and fit each where it belongs — the first catches plain steam's condensate, the second catches the plain steam that superheated degrades into.%n%nBoth hatches §3auto-output§r: attach a pipe, send the water back to the boiler, and the loop closes.%n%nFit them and read the books again — every drop of burned steam came home.%n%n§3No water on the floor, no steam wasted.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§6§lLight the Geothermal Boiler
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=Acceptance: craft the §3Large Geothermal Steam Boiler§r controller yourself — the panel only checks it, and it stays yours.%n%nMatch the §3casing, pipe, gearbox and frame§r in one tier and leave the controller slot at the front; hook up a magma pump and a steady water source, throw the switch, and your first steam well starts breathing.%n%nWant superheated? From steel on, slot a Geothermal Overheat Chip into the controller to switch over.%n%n§2One geothermal well, steam around the clock.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§6§lChoose Your Wells
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=The three wells meet — selection time: geothermal eats §3capital§r but runs steady round the clock once the magma plumbing is in; solar runs §1full by day, zero by night§r and wants reservoirs to shave the peaks; the Gear Steam Compressor converts §6steam surplus§r into superheated on demand — the most flexible, and the hungriest for volume.%n%nThere is no standard answer, only fit or misfit — ratio them to your base's veins, weather and steam balance.%n%n§8§oAdults, of course, take all three.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§3§lDrilling 101
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=Settle the Steam Fluid Drill's oil ledger before you dig: bronze wells start small and modest, steel wells start the same but climb multiples further — the curves live in the tooltip.%n%nStructural discipline is strict: exactly §11§r steam input hatch — bring two and the shape refuses to form.%n%nSurvey the field before raising the derrick, and lay the tanks before the oil arrives; the order matters.%n%n§3One good well, half an oil field.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§3§lThree Kiln Brothers
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=The kiln district assembles its three brothers: §3the Reinforced Brick Blast Furnace, the Large Coke Oven and the Crust Steam Borer§r — three machines, three temperaments.%n%nThe blast furnace's §3heat§r is the delicate one: it climbs while running, sags while idle, and once the fire is right, speed and parallelism rise together — never let it go cold. The coke oven heats slowly and cools even slower, a game of patience; the borer speeds up outright on superheated and rolls its ores from a void-drop table.%n%nThe details differ; the common point does not: all three must be fed.%n%n§8§oFire all three and the neighbors think you brew elixirs.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§3§lA Furnace Fed by Fire
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=The Siemens-Martin is picky by birth: §csuperheated steam only§r — plain steam cannot even get in the door. Preheat is its hungriest hour; past the line the appetite settles, and the hotter it burns, the thriftier it drinks. It also demands §3air§r — check the gas line before this furnace starts work.%n%nThe hotter the hearth, the harder recipe times get shaved — capped at half; parallelism grows with it, and the better you feed it, the more steel pours out.%n%nChapter B's compressor gate was built for exactly this fire-tiger.%n%n§3Steel by the ton begins with taming the beast.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§5§lHub Logistics
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=The hub logistics era opens. The system has three layers: §5hubs§r for bulk move, §5cache nodes§r for caching and dispatch, §5terminals§r for the pocket. A hub only truly transfers once a §dHub Singularity Chip§r is fitted.%n%nFor exact rules and capacities, trust the machine tooltips — this system keeps evolving, so here is a map, not a ruler.%n%nNode binding, cross-chunk and cross-dimensional details come in their own branches.%n%n§8§oFrom today, pipes are decoration.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§3§lFurnace, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=Acceptance: the Large Steam Furnace controller is the proof.%n%nEven the bronze tier feeds a whole base's smelting, every chamber drawing from one steam main; casing, pipe, gearbox and frame form in one tier.%n%nTier-ups later need no re-plumbing — leave headroom on the main and you will never redo a pipe.%n%n§2One furnace line feeds a whole bronze base.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§3§lAir Compressor, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=Acceptance: the Air Compressor controller is the proof.%n%nIt upgrades §6air supply§r from a pump workshop to an industrial main: the Atmospheric Centrifuge, the Siemens-Martin and the Ammonia Plant all queue downstream for gas — size the main to the downstream peak.%n%nAnd leave room for air tanks — the bigger the bank, the steadier the buffer, the calmer the downstream. Air freedom is the first step of chemical freedom.%n%n§2When the blowers spin, the money rolls in.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§3§lThe Rare Gas Gate
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=Acceptance: the Atmospheric Centrifuge controller plus a Rare Gas Separation Chip — those two are the proof.%n%nSteel plus chip is what actually opens the door to §3krypton, xenon, neon and helium§r — the first sip of the glow-component chain and the deeper tech beyond.%n%nWorth repeating, because it bears repeating: the chip only works on steel — on a bronze unit it is an expensive souvenir.%n%n§2Rare-gas independence starts here.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§3§lFour Modes, One Climb
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=The drill runs four output modes — §3water, distilled water, brine, magma§r — each with its own yield; picking a mode is picking an output rate. Ratios and steam costs live in the tooltip.%n%nEfficiency climbs in §1points§r: every cycle banks a little, and only a full bank counts as full efficiency — a fresh well pumps nothing because it is still warming up.%n%n§cMode switching is steel-only, and switching resets efficiency on the spot§r — decide before you touch it, and never let a hard-won ramp go to waste.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§3§lThe Kilns, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=Acceptance: the controllers of the Reinforced Brick Blast Furnace, the Large Coke Oven and the Crust Steam Borer — all three together make the proof.%n%nSteel, coke and ores: three lines firing together; leave each its own spare branch on the steam main.%n%nThe borer's void-drop table coughs up surprises now and then — a hopper underneath keeps the luck off the floor.%n%n§2Kiln district lit: the bronze base is properly industrial now.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§3§lSiemens-Martin, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Acceptance: the Siemens-Martin Furnace controller is the proof.%n%nBefore ignition, confirm both the §6superheated main§r and the §6air main§r reach its door: missing either, it never survives the preheat. Preheat is its hungriest stretch — leave headroom on the mains ahead of time.%n%nOnce accepted, light it and start production — from that day on, steel is counted in tons.%n%n§2The day the furnace runs full, the warehouse is the bottleneck.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§d§lSingularity Depths
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=Singularities become hard currency here — the deepest stretch of the current build. The chain: the §dSteam Singularity Entangler§r mass-produces them, the §dDense State Steam Manipulator§r presses a thousand into one dense variant, the §dCritical Entangled Singularity Stabilizer§r presses further into critical, and the §dSingularity Drilling Hub§r burns them for work.%n%nFrom this chapter on, every bill is counted in §dsingularities§r — steam becomes small change.%n%nNo need to clear chapters C and D: past the mid-line gate and the hub-logistics gateway, the singularity opens to you.%n%n§3The deepest point so far is steam collapsing into itself.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=§5§lTwo Reservoirs
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=The hub reservoirs hold astronomical numbers: pressure cells stack the base layer by layer, and Hub Singularity Chips multiply it further — §1the reinforced chip's multiplier wins when both are fitted§r. Exact figures live in the tooltip; here is just the direction.%n%nThe water side stores and dispenses too; §3overflow is automatic, but the stockpile is banked by hand§r — past the threshold, overflow opens.%n%n§8§oThis is not a reservoir. This is a sea.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=§5§lSix Cache Nodes
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=Nodes are the logistics network's capillaries — choosing right beats piling more: the steam and fluid families each come in three tiers, capacity and rate stepping up together, with adjustable rate steps to fine-tune for each downstream's appetite — numbers in the tooltip.%n%nBinding costs vary by tier: some run §dzero-singularity§r, stronger tiers burn more, and the overpressure tier wants hub and chips all in place — the price list lives in the tooltips.%n%n§3Small nodes, big shoes, spread like stars.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=§3§lPyrolyze the Vein
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=No need to pump the vein to the surface: the Vein Steam Pyrolyzer sits right on the oil field and §3cracks it in place§r, skipping the pipeline entirely. Its finest virtue is §3backfill§r — every cycle returns part of the fluid to the chunk, so mining never drains the ledger and the vein steadies with use.%n%nRange chips grow its territory: upgrading absorbs the tier below outright, no sunk costs; the voltage gate climbs step by step and the appetite grows with it.%n%nPyrolyzer plus drill is the oil region's double insurance.%n%n§8§oTake and give back — the vein becomes an old friend.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=§3§lThe Drill, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=Acceptance: the Steam Fluid Drill controller is the proof.%n%nOnce more on the §6two-input ban§r: exactly one steam input hatch, not one more; the same-tier casing rule applies as ever.%n%nAt full efficiency a single steel well feeds an entire pyrolysis-and-refining chain; the moment the acceptance piece lands, the oil field goes to work.%n%n§2One steel well outdraws a whole tank farm — no more shortages.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.name=§d§lEntangle the Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.desc=The Steam Singularity Entangler is where singularities are born: the harder you feed it, the faster heat banks — but with §3diminishing returns§r; past a point, every extra liter buys less.%n%nThree grades, three work tempos — plain, superheated, supercritical, each brisker than the last. It only ships when heat is full, then clears and starts over, and §ca clogged output bus means a sit-down strike§r.%n%nHow much to feed it? Let your steam balance do the talking.%n%n§8§oIt is not picky about food — only about portion size.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.name=§d§lA Wild Singularity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.desc=Wild singularities generate only in the §3Overworld and the Nether§r, at a tear-jerkingly sparse density — meeting one is pure legwork and luck.%n%nThe threshold is mercifully low: bare hands will do. But a dropped plain singularity §1detonates seconds after landing§r — it hurts entities, not blocks.%n%nThe critical kind is far worse: a shorter fuse, §cblocks and all§r, and it scatters more small singularities with fuses of their own.%n%n§cDo not count your singularities on the floor.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.name=§3§lReborn in Electricity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.desc=This chapter is steam's strength reborn as electricity-era convenience: the §3Kinetic Processing Array§r folds advanced recipes into a single line, the §3Mega Steam Turbine Array§r burns steam straight into EU, and the §3Crust Matter Aggregator§r and the §3Cluster§r pull mining and processing under one roof.%n%nThey still run on steam — just at absurd scales, so your reservoirs and mains grow with them.%n%nAlong the main line through hub logistics and the singularity depths, this chapter awaits — the road is long, so make home comfortable first.%n%n§8§oConvenience is technology at its most considerate.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.name=§5§lThe Hubs, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.desc=Acceptance: the Steam Hub Array and the Water Hub Array controllers — both together make the proof.%n%nSteam-side auto-output means downstream machines never see the word “thirsty” again; the water side dispatches the whole base's condensate from one common bank.%n%nAnd do chip both: §cwithout chips they only store§r. Two pieces, both required.%n%n§2Reservoirs up — the base's steam heartbeat is steady.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.name=§5§lTerminals and Hub Chips
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.desc=The Hub Terminal is a remote control for your pocket: hold it to §1teleport across dimensions§r, burning singularities by the distance — the farther you go, the pricier the ticket.%n%nHub chips boost the hubs: §1×5§r and §1×20§r tiers, reinforced over plain. The Reinforced Hub Singularity Chip is one of the priciest single recipes in the pack: a base of singularities, circuits and dense plates riding along, a bottle of radon soaked in, then slow-crafted on a high-tier assembler.%n%n§8§oThis is not crafting, it is a mortgage — paid in installments, and the singularities don't stay.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.name=§5§lFour Singularity Compartments
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.desc=All four singularity compartments together make the proof: two for steam and two for fluids, capacity and throughput mirroring each other — the panel only checks, and all four stay yours.%n%nThey are the hub network's §dhigh-throughput gates§r: place one at each end of a line, one swallowing, one emitting — no pipe in between, and neither distance nor dimension is an argument.%n%nMind the facing: each of the four has its own flow direction, and §creversed means dead§r.%n%n§2One gate at each end — the horizon becomes a neighbor.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.name=§5§lThe 600-Tick Rebind
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.desc=Node registration has a heartbeat: after a successful registration, an §3idempotent recheck§r runs at a fixed interval to confirm the binding holds; on failure it drops into high-frequency retries and never gives up.%n%nThe registration itself carries §3cross-dimensional chunk loading§r, so remote nodes take effect at once across dimensions; the machine keeps its own time, and a steady heartbeat means a steady network.%n%n§cBreaking a node refunds no singularity — the consumption marker stays, no freeloading.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.name=§3§lPyrolyzer, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.desc=Acceptance: the Vein Steam Pyrolyzer controller and its §3T1 range chip§r — those two are the proof.%n%nThe moment the chip goes in, the whole vein answers to it; later tier upgrades absorb the one below — no sunk costs.%n%nBackfill keeps the field stable while the drill feeds it from the other side; kit complete, the pyrolysis line opens.%n%n§2The oil field becomes a printing press.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.name=§d§lThe Entangler, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.desc=Acceptance: the Steam Singularity Entangler controller is the proof.%n%nIts output is a volume-for-singularities trade, worth a dedicated reservoir line — one line to feed it, one warehouse to receive; keep the output bus clear or production simply stops.%n%nSuperheated and supercritical feed cut the cycle again and again — the difference in mass-production is night and day.%n%n§2Singularities clock in for shifts now — mass production begins.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.name=§d§lFirst Singularity, Banked
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.desc=The hard currency makes its first deposit: dug from the wild or grown in the entangler, provenance is not questioned — one will do.%n%nEvery later bill — hub chips, node bindings, dense pressing, the critical leap — snowballs from this first one; the wild route and the factory route converge here.%n%nDon't spend the two from the reward carelessly: they are the opening balance of your singularity account.%n%n§dShow one, receive two: the first bucket of gold lands.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.name=§3§lThe Kinetic Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.desc=The Kinetic Processing Array is today's master of steam thrift, and its core virtue is one word: save. It takes §csuperheated steam only§r — plain steam need not apply; the energy discount digs deeper with gear tiers, pipe tiers squeeze recipe times, and parallelism grows with tier and stacks.%n%nThe steam rate also slides as voltage climbs — §3the higher the tier, the thriftier§r. Tinker with the tier setup twice and the feel comes fast; details in the tooltip.%n%nEvery liter saved is pure profit.%n%n§3One KPA replaces a machine hall.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.name=§3§lThe Mega Turbine Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.desc=The Mega Steam Turbine Array (MSTA) burns steam back into EU — the pack's only true power plant. Efficiency caps scale with grade: §1the richer the grade, the sweeter the EU§r; the tier table lives in the tooltip.%n%nSupply priority is written in stone: §3dense supercritical > supercritical > dense superheated > dense > superheated > plain§r; the higher grades also demand a proper hull tier.%n%n§cThe explosion clause is equally stone-written: total dynamo output below the demanded EU, and it blows on the spot§r — do the safety math before ignition.%n%n§8§oIt makes power, and it makes a scene.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.name=§3§lCrust Matter, Aggregated
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.desc=The Crust Matter Aggregator's bill looks dense but is only three layers of multiplication — mode, dimension slots and filters, each multiplying its own share. The formula lives in the tooltip; here you learn to see the layers.%n%nBilling splits into a §3plain tier and a dense tier§r, worlds apart; targeted mode filters out exactly what you lack, refreshing the ore pool when switched.%n%nThe fortune ceiling follows the currency: §1bare, singularity, critical singularity§r — one ceiling per tier.%n%n§8§oThe last step of digging through the crust is making the crust walk up to you.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.name=§3§lClusters and Ten Chain Steps
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.desc=The Cluster is the biggest single machine in the current build, and the steam ledger's final exam: chain steam swells §3geometrically§r with chain length, capped by a step limit; fixed steam bills by tier multiplier — formulas live in the tooltip.%n%nThree rules of care: preheat before start; idling and starvation both bleed status, and §cstarvation hurts more than shutdown§r; lubricant and logistics modules drain continuously by tier — keep the feed steady.%n%nThe §1ten chain steps§r run from crushing to smelting, each with its own tempo.%n%n§8§oThis is not a factory. It is a pipe organ that breathes.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.name=§3§lAmmonia and Seven Catalysts
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.desc=The Ammonia Plant is heavy industry's grand finale: preheat already eats well, the running bill climbs another step, and parallels stack it higher — the fiercest single-machine steam bill in the pack hangs here; exact rates live in the tooltip.%n%nSeven catalysts unlock seven recipe routes, and the plant tips superheated steam back as a byproduct gift; do not feed it before preheat completes.%n%n§dWith ammonia and catalysis online, every downstream production line has its rations secured.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.name=§5§lFull-Network Check
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.desc=Chapter D closes: put the §3chip–node–terminal§r three layers in place and the full-network check begins.%n%nChips in the hubs, nodes bound to the hubs, terminal in hand; when the batch rounds flow steady and the cache nodes start breathing, the network counts as alive — for the heartbeat rhythm, revisit the registration lesson.%n%nAll four branches' acceptance pieces are on you — the perfect moment to wire it all together.%n%n§8§oThe moment the logistics graph connects beats any boss fight.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.name=§5§lThe Nodes, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.desc=Acceptance: the Steam Cache Node and the Universal Fluid Cache Node — those two are the proof, two ambassadors of the §dzero-singularity§r family.%n%nNot one singularity spent, and steam and fluid buffering reach a thousand blocks away; rates tune to each downstream's appetite, supplying whatever is missing, however far out it is.%n%nExpansion is free and plug-and-play; cut your teeth on these before stepping up to the reinforced tiers.%n%n§2Logistics freedom starts at zero cost.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.name=§d§lDense at 1000 to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.desc=The Dense State Steam Manipulator presses §11000§r singularities into one dense variant and decompresses back a thousandfold — the §3master dispatcher§r of steam grades across the whole chain.%n%nFuel bills settle per unit and stay modest; the machine always validates the fluid before charging fuel — nothing burns in vain. Tier switches convert the accumulator and keep it — §2changing gears never wipes the ledger§r. For the fine print and rates, read the tooltip.%n%n§8§oThe romance of density: a warehouse pressed into a pocket.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.name=§d§lThe Critical Compressor
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.desc=The Critical Entangled Singularity Stabilizer eats §ddense variants only§r: plain steam is first pressed a thousandfold by the manipulator, then pressed again here into a §dcritical singularity§r — dense is the ticket, critical the trophy.%n%nIt is a slow craft: sipping dense steam mouthful by mouthful until the vault is full, with the whole chain's priciest point at this machine's far end; rates live in the tooltip. If your fortune is thin, get the entangler's mass-production line humming first.%n%n§3Critical is a whole steam age pressed into a point.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.name=§d§lThe Singularity Drill Hub
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.desc=The Singularity Drilling Hub is the singularity era's first working machine, and its bill is the plainest: a base diet of §6superheated steam§r with §cno speedup at all§r — here superheated is only the ticket in, never the throttle.%n%nEvery active node bills on top: drilling and mining nodes each carry their own price list, with radius, fortune and pace all buyable for singularities; and every binding costs §done singularity§r.%n%n§8§oThe more you bind, the bigger the appetite — settle the catering before it starts work.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.name=§3§lKPA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.desc=Acceptance: the Kinetic Processing Array controller is the proof.%n%nThe §1energy discount§r stacked with §1packed parallelism§r makes it the central kitchen of the book's advanced recipes; a fed §6superheated main§r is the only prerequisite.%n%nGear and pipe tiers switch freely to match each recipe's tempo — one line runs the whole recipe book.%n%n§2With enough steam it beats a whole machine hall for peace of mind.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.name=§3§lMSTA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.desc=Acceptance: the Mega Steam Turbine Array controller is the proof.%n%nDo the safety math before ignition: if the dynamo banks' combined output cannot cover the array's demanded EU, §cit blows on the spot§r — fit enough banks, then throw the switch.%n%nThere is no shortcut around this arithmetic, and it doubles as the template for every big machine that follows — work it out once, use it everywhere.%n%n§8§oArithmetic is safety; mental math saves lives.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.name=§3§lCycle Overlimit
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.desc=Acceptance: one §dcritical steam-entangled singularity§r is the proof, and the panel only checks, never keeps — the mega turbine's singularity mode is waiting for exactly this kind of meal.%n%nIt also holds a §dcycle overlimit§r ace: with a Cycle Overlimit Chip fitted and all dynamo banks stacked, the output multiplier keeps climbing, EU/L scaling with it, while steam consumption §2stays put§r — a free slice of power.%n%nCheck your dynamo headroom before fitting; don't overdraft the safety margin along with the output.%n%n§8§oAn engineer's romance is running past nameplate.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.name=§3§lCMA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.desc=Acceptance: the Crust Matter Aggregator controller is the proof.%n%nThe §3dense tier's§r entry fee is startlingly cheap, the output anything but: a weight-targeted mineral buffet; dimension slots pull other dimensions into the mining claim, and filters distill the output into the list you actually want.%n%nA critical singularity tops fortune at its ceiling — whatever you lack, target-filter exactly that.%n%n§2The crust is the warehouse; the filter is the pick list.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.name=§3§lThe Cluster, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.desc=Acceptance: the master controller and Processing Cluster Logistics Module of the §3Steam-Powered Mineral Processing Logistics Engineering Cluster§r — both together make the proof.%n%nController in hand, logistics module in tow, the §1ten-step§r pipeline takes shape here: intake, crushing and washing strung straight through to smelted goods — just keep the lubricant flowing.%n%nChain steam inflates step by step; size the main for the deepest chain you run. Preheat before start, and never starve it mid-run.%n%n§2One building, one whole mine.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.name=§d§lThe Manipulator, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.desc=Acceptance: the Dense State Steam Manipulator controller is the proof.%n%nIt is the steam ladder's §3elevator§r: press a thousand shares into one and save astronomical capacity; decompress upward to feed the machines that want plain grades.%n%nFuel settles per unit, tier switches keep the accumulation — tinker as you please, nothing is lost.%n%n§2One-thousand-to-one, industrialized at last.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.name=§d§lCritical Singularity Get
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.desc=Acceptance: the Critical Entangled Singularity Stabilizer controller and one §dcritical singularity§r — both together make the proof, and the panel only checks, never keeps.%n%nThe critical kind is the chain's §dhighest-denomination hard currency§r: the drill hub, the mega turbines and the aggregator all name it for their top tiers — you can never hold too many.%n%nIf one lies around unclaimed, reread the explosion clauses a couple of quests back.%n%n§8§oHold it steady. Don't shake.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.name=§d§lDrill Hub, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.desc=Acceptance: the Singularity Drilling Hub plus its drilling and mining nodes — together they make the proof.%n%nThe superheated base appetite scales linearly with node count — settle the quota with your compressor and reservoirs first.%n%nUpgraded nodes burn §dsingularities§r for fortune and radius; the mine spreads wilder, the output snowballs. Quota agreed, the mine opens.%n%n§2A singularity-driven mine never sleeps.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.name=§3§lMake Steam Great Again!
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.desc=The wrap-up inventory: a full sweep of all §623§r steam multiblocks — from the first puff of the bronze Air Compressor to a Critical Singularity worth §d4 billion liters of steam equivalent§r.%n%nAll four branches accepted; looking back, every step was paved by steam itself. The four acceptance pieces are the best souvenirs.%n%n§8§oSomeone asks about electricity? We say: steam IS electricity.§r
# BQ quests END

