lore.entry.biomes.steppe.title=Rusted Steppe
lore.entry.biomes.steppe.p0=Old roads crossed the grass sea. Valve seats and milestones greeted travelers long before city walls.
lore.entry.biomes.steppe.p1=Look across open ground for shelters, switchhouses and camps. Night echoes and ruin guardians keep different watches.
lore.entry.biomes.forest.title=Gearwork Forest
lore.entry.biomes.forest.p0=Roots curl around rivets; the canopy swallows factory outlines. The timber remembers rooms never finished.
lore.entry.biomes.forest.p1=Archive kiosks, sap collectors and gear gardens preserve daily life. Lamps and pipe pieces are architecture, not evidence of working machines.
lore.entry.biomes.wastes.title=Brass Wastes
lore.entry.biomes.wastes.p0=Cold chimneys still seem to await the wind. The black soil preserves the last shift, not its heat.
lore.entry.biomes.wastes.p1=Watch for furnace basins, aid trenches and observation sheds. Leave warning rings and marked impact points before striking back.
lore.entry.biomes.swamp.title=Fumarole Swamp
lore.entry.biomes.swamp.p0=Water presses old bells beneath the mud. Walkways once led people out of the flood; now they mark the banks.
lore.entry.biomes.swamp.p1=Seek grotto caches in newly generated terrain. Upgrading does not insert these sites into old chunks.
lore.entry.biomes.rivers.title=Forgotten River and Withered Riverbed
lore.entry.biomes.rivers.p0=The Forgotten River preserves the haulers' promise of another dock; the Withered Riverbed lays a waterless route across the ground. Rivers once carried coal, copper and letters to the works, and rails beneath broken bridges still remember their course beside water.
lore.entry.biomes.rivers.p1=Approach pumps, aqueducts and signal bridges from dry banks. Decorative valves and pipes imply no fluid recipe.
lore.entry.biomes.lake.title=Forgotten Lake
lore.entry.biomes.lake.p0=Forgotten Lake uses the existing water-system biome identity; this topic records its lake shape, island and shore. The island bears the final royal court. Its shore is no perfect circle; water and old land leave separate boundaries.
lore.entry.biomes.lake.p1=Find the tree's ascending branch road. After clearing one room, its empty royal bar tracks the remaining guards; an oath fragment guides you to a guard in that court.
lore.entry.structures.fallen_foundry.title=Fallen Foundry
lore.entry.structures.fallen_foundry.p0=A compact foundry stands in a gearwork forest clearing. Its reception room, service workshop and sealed archive lead to the casting hall. Supplies remain in wall-side crates; readable consoles hold the last shift records. Beyond the workshop waits the Colossus.
lore.entry.structures.fallen_foundry.p1=With the workshop guards defeated, the foundry finally falls quiet. The accident log names no final worker, only the pressure before shutdown. The Colossus still treats intruders as runaway furnace stock. Its copper shock rings, fissures and falling anvils leave the same narrow escapes the workers once used.
lore.entry.structures.fallen_foundry.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.subsided_factory.title=Subsided Factory
lore.entry.structures.subsided_factory.p0=The meadow factory has subsided by a single shallow level. Stairs join its receiving hall, screening workshop and main plant. Uncollected supplies remain in wall-side crates. Shift consoles describe production recovery, but the equipment has become another way for the Hive to grow.
lore.entry.structures.subsided_factory.p1=After the workshop enemies fall, the screening machinery grows quiet. The recorded flow of waste follows the mycelium toward the Hive. Watch spore marks and spreading lines. Resonance leaves inner and outer safe zones; sustained damage can interrupt its limited repair.
lore.entry.structures.subsided_factory.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.boiler_shrine.title=Boiler Shrine
lore.entry.structures.boiler_shrine.p0=Three pressure pedestals support the boiler nave, with service courts on either side. Stability became a gospel; leaks disappeared from its records.
lore.entry.structures.boiler_shrine.p1=Clear the three steam districts and close their main valves to awaken the core. Each isolated pedestal has a cache; the final chest awaits the Spiral.
lore.entry.structures.boiler_shrine.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.weaving_mill.title=Weaving Mill
lore.entry.structures.weaving_mill.p0=Yarn stores, looms and overhead conveyors lie beneath sawtooth roofs. The ledger counts fabric; the shift book repeats an unsent letter.
lore.entry.structures.weaving_mill.p1=Clear the workshops, restore the first two circuits, then connect both final relays in order. The Weaver awakens at the loom core; side routes bypass the main hall.
lore.entry.structures.weaving_mill.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.sniper_watch.title=Riftstring Watch
lore.entry.structures.sniper_watch.p0=Stepped towers climb the hillside above ammunition vaults and observation rooms. Their sights still follow a railway that carries no trains.
lore.entry.structures.sniper_watch.p1=Clear the three calibration stations and align their instruments to awaken the Sniper. Tower rooms, bridge piers and side ramps provide cover.
lore.entry.structures.sniper_watch.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.mirror_barracks.title=Mirror Barracks
lore.entry.structures.mirror_barracks.p0=Two barracks face each other across a broken bridge above a buried armory. Opposing orders bear the same signature.
lore.entry.structures.mirror_barracks.p1=Clear both wings and release the two bridge gates to awaken the Mirror Guard. Armory routes remain open; district and final caches unlock separately.
lore.entry.structures.mirror_barracks.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.resonant_station.title=Resonant Station
lore.entry.structures.resonant_station.p0=Three resonant stages surround a railway clock hall. Its last recorded chime came a full night after the official shutdown.
lore.entry.structures.resonant_station.p1=Clear all three stages and sound low, middle, then high. A wrong note resets the sequence without restoring defeated guards.
lore.entry.structures.resonant_station.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.switchhouse.title=Switchhouse
lore.entry.structures.switchhouse.p0=A relay tower marks a rescue train beside the twin-line switchhouse. Sneak-right-click its plates to inspect arrival, return and rescue circuits.
lore.entry.structures.switchhouse.p1=Connect the three circuits in their marked order to open the cache. The surviving record reveals that the official line stopped the rescue train.
lore.entry.structures.pumping_house.title=Pumping House
lore.entry.structures.pumping_house.p0=A relief bypass links the intake to an elevated pump. The plate warns: vent pressure, open the bypass, then start the pump.
lore.entry.structures.pumping_house.p1=Restore the valve chain to unseal the service cache. A crossed-out supply order reads on its back: do not send water to the empty city.
lore.entry.structures.workers_lodging.title=Workers' Shelter
lore.entry.structures.workers_lodging.p0=There are no guards here: only beds, a kitchen and two shift records. Read the entrance board, then find the shelter room.
lore.entry.structures.workers_lodging.p1=The official account says everyone left. The dishes and workbadge abandoned beside the beds tell a different ending.
lore.entry.structures.shore_crane.title=Shore Crane
lore.entry.structures.shore_crane.p0=A crane reaches over the loading pit above a shore-side pile bridge. Follow dock, cabin and loading platform to read the driver’s route.
lore.entry.structures.shore_crane.p1=The final crate was never dispatched. The driver kept it for a family whose names remain on the cabin desk.
lore.entry.structures.cold_altar.title=Cold Altar
lore.entry.structures.cold_altar.p0=Three damaged furnaces hold black soot, pale ash and red rust. Inspect their plates and choose the furnace marked with cold ash.
lore.entry.structures.cold_altar.p1=The cold-ash choice opens the rear cache. The final shutdown was a deliberate act to hide the ember from an order.
lore.entry.structures.cold_altar.record=The last page is preserved in the Chronicle. You have followed the path this story left behind.
lore.entry.structures.trench_infirmary.title=Trench Infirmary
lore.entry.structures.trench_infirmary.p0=Two records remain in the braced trench clinic: treatment room and medicine cabinet. Follow the curtained ward to its final entry.
lore.entry.structures.trench_infirmary.p1=The medic crossed out every allegiance mark. The last dose went to a wounded soldier from the opposing trench.
lore.entry.structures.ash_crematory.title=Ash Crematory
lore.entry.structures.ash_crematory.p0=Twin furnaces, flues and ash carts form a strangely quiet works. Three ash guards protect a nameless list.
lore.entry.structures.ash_crematory.p1=Defeat all three guards and reach the ash cache. The final space on the list eventually took the recorder’s own name.
lore.entry.structures.rift_observatory.title=Rift Observatory
lore.entry.structures.rift_observatory.p0=Three mirrors in the hilltop station are marked near, middle and far. Align their fixed scales rather than chasing the shifting sky.
lore.entry.structures.rift_observatory.p1=The aligned mirrors reveal a cache. The final report records no rift: only the date the observer stood here.
lore.entry.structures.rift_observatory.record=The last page is preserved in the Chronicle. You have followed the path this story left behind.
lore.entry.structures.weighbridge.title=Weighbridge
lore.entry.structures.weighbridge.p0=Twin weighing rails flank a scale office and a hidden channel. Three raiders guard ledgers whose totals never match.
lore.entry.structures.weighbridge.p1=Defeat the three raiders and reach the duty cabinet. The missing grain was quietly diverted to unlisted refugees.
lore.entry.structures.valve_yard.title=Valve Yard
lore.entry.structures.valve_yard.p0=The gauges read twenty, eighty and sixty. Keep the low-pressure bypass open and close the two higher-pressure valves.
lore.entry.structures.valve_yard.p1=The cache holds an order to lock every safety valve. The engineer who left this test was the only one who refused to sign it.
lore.entry.structures.archivist_kiosk.title=Archivist Kiosk
lore.entry.structures.archivist_kiosk.p0=This quiet kiosk holds a damaged cabinet and a buried backup room. Compare the official and handwritten records of the same day.
lore.entry.structures.archivist_kiosk.p1=Their dates match; their endings do not. The backup preserves names the official archive erased.
lore.entry.structures.sap_collector.title=Sap Collector
lore.entry.structures.sap_collector.p0=A collection trough leads to a hillside root service bay. Follow the workstation to the roots: the last living part of the machinery.
lore.entry.structures.sap_collector.p1=Production called the trees fuel. The service book demanded their protection; its last keeper closed the valve.
lore.entry.structures.mire_boardwalk.title=Mire Boardwalk
lore.entry.structures.mire_boardwalk.p0=A bent pile walkway follows the wet margin to a sounding hut. Read the entrance, bend and hut markers; there is no required combat.
lore.entry.structures.mire_boardwalk.p1=The old retreat arrow pointed deeper into the mire. Someone corrected it and led the last group along the supported boards.
lore.entry.structures.pilgrim_arch.title=Pilgrim Arch
lore.entry.structures.pilgrim_arch.p0=A broken arch, roadside offerings and a shelter cave border the old road. Two sentries and a hunter still demand obsolete passes.
lore.entry.structures.pilgrim_arch.p1=Defeat all three and reach the far side. When passes became warrants, a keeper finally let the undocumented through.
lore.entry.structures.pilgrim_arch.record=The last page is preserved in the Chronicle. You have followed the path this story left behind.
lore.entry.structures.signal_bridge.title=Signal Bridge
lore.entry.structures.signal_bridge.p0=Three signal plates remain beside the bridge and service tower. The intact plate records tower, bridge, then road.
lore.entry.structures.signal_bridge.p1=Restoring the sequence opens the bridgehead cache. A corrupted call once brought artillery instead of aid.
lore.entry.structures.fungus_cellar.title=Fungus Cellar
lore.entry.structures.fungus_cellar.p0=Light enters a twin-stair cellar through its broken roof. Three hive-born guards surround bags whose contents have learned to remember.
lore.entry.structures.fungus_cellar.p1=Defeat the three guards and reach the purification bench. The keeper kept counting sacks long after they ceased to be food.
lore.entry.structures.boiler_chapel.title=Boiler Chapel
lore.entry.structures.boiler_chapel.p0=Three bells—outer, inner and master—stand below organ pipes and a broken dome. Read their plates and proceed inward.
lore.entry.structures.boiler_chapel.p1=The outer, inner and master bells release the altar cache. The final prayer became a shutdown command that saved the crew.
lore.entry.structures.broken_aqueduct.title=Broken Aqueduct
lore.entry.structures.broken_aqueduct.p0=The damaged aqueduct follows a contour above a service room. Read the inlet’s old waterline, then explore beneath the break.
lore.entry.structures.broken_aqueduct.p1=The water never stopped; it bypassed the empty city. By the final repair, its list of residents no longer changed.
lore.entry.structures.gear_garden.title=Gear Garden
lore.entry.structures.gear_garden.p0=A vertical gear tower and stepped planters ring a garden path. Three echoes protect machinery that no longer drives anything.
lore.entry.structures.gear_garden.p1=Defeat all three and reach the core cache. The last mechanic converted the workstation into a garden and called watering it maintenance.
lore.entry.structures.expedition_camp.title=Expedition Camp
lore.entry.structures.expedition_camp.p0=Hillside tents, a supply cave and a lookout retain the final departure list. Read the map tent, then follow the campfire record.
lore.entry.structures.expedition_camp.p1=The return list is much shorter. The final line on the map marks a way home, not a new frontier.
lore.entry.structures.mire_grotto_cache.title=Mire Grotto Cache
lore.entry.structures.mire_grotto_cache.p0=A shallow grotto and dry landing shelter the surveyor above the waterline.
lore.entry.structures.mire_grotto_cache.p1=The special cache preserves a sounding weight; the actual site event confirms the exploration record.
lore.entry.structures.mire_grotto_cache.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.city_archive_cache.title=City Archive Cache
lore.entry.structures.city_archive_cache.p0=A sealed room in the old city never received the final signature on its removal list.
lore.entry.structures.city_archive_cache.p1=Its special cache holds an archive tube. Old chunks do not receive this room automatically.
lore.entry.structures.city_archive_cache.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.structures.rail_service_cache.title=Rail Service Cache
lore.entry.structures.rail_service_cache.p0=A tool desk and a short track record repair work, not a promise of passage anywhere.
lore.entry.structures.rail_service_cache.p1=Its special cache holds a repair token; repeated right clicks do not regenerate its one-time record reward.
lore.entry.structures.rail_service_cache.record=Your journey has confirmed this account.
lore.entry.items.oath_fragment.title=Oath Fragment
lore.entry.items.oath_fragment.p0=An oathguard's broken seal: a post may stand empty, but never its promise.
lore.entry.items.oath_fragment.p1=Left by a defeated oathguard; right-click to find a living guard in the same court.
lore.entry.items.old_crown.title=Old Crown
lore.entry.items.old_crown.p0=First keepsake. The crown is silent; the roots remember its weight.
lore.entry.items.old_crown.p1=Left by the defeated king. Possessing it does not grant a participant's achievement permissions.
lore.entry.items.brass_chronicle.title=Brass Chronicle
lore.entry.items.brass_chronicle.p0=Sand erased its date, but not the artisan's marks.
lore.entry.items.brass_chronicle.p1=A historical record preserved in the archivist-kiosk cache.
lore.entry.items.patina_seal.title=Patina Seal
lore.entry.items.patina_seal.p0=An old steam inspector's seal, retaining the shape of duty.
lore.entry.items.patina_seal.p1=Earned by defeating Tarnished Spiral at the boiler shrine.
lore.entry.items.sigh_glass.title=Sigh Glass
lore.entry.items.sigh_glass.p0=The steppe's wind is caught in a crack.
lore.entry.items.sigh_glass.p1=An observation relic from the rift-observatory cache.
lore.entry.items.mire_memory.title=Mire Memory
lore.entry.items.mire_memory.p0=Deep in the mire, a leaf keeps the sunlight of that day.
lore.entry.items.mire_memory.p1=A memory of the banks preserved in the mire-boardwalk cache.
lore.entry.items.royal_sap.title=Royal Sap
lore.entry.items.royal_sap.p0=Jade resin from the great tree, like an unspoken promise.
lore.entry.items.royal_sap.p1=A narrative relic from the sap-collector cache.
lore.entry.items.broken_edict.title=Broken Edict
lore.entry.items.broken_edict.p0=Only the last words remain: I am still here.
lore.entry.items.broken_edict.p1=An old order from the boiler-chapel cache.
lore.entry.items.switchyard_key.title=Switchyard Key
lore.entry.items.switchyard_key.p0=All the wear lies on one side of the brass handle, as if its owner changed the final switch before going home.
lore.entry.items.switchyard_key.p1=The switchhouse cache preserves this token of railway dispatch.
item.prosperity.switchyard_key.name=Switchyard Key
lore.relic.switchyard_key=All the wear lies on one side of the brass handle, as if its owner changed the final switch before going home.
lore.entry.items.pump_valve_core.title=Pump Valve Core
lore.entry.items.pump_valve_core.p0=A ring of residue marks the old waterline; it once held an unseen pressure for an entire district.
lore.entry.items.pump_valve_core.p1=Find it in the pumping-house cache as a record of waterworks and industry.
item.prosperity.pump_valve_core.name=Pump Valve Core
lore.relic.pump_valve_core=A ring of residue marks the old waterline; it once held an unseen pressure for an entire district.
lore.entry.items.cold_furnace_ember.title=Cold Furnace Ember
lore.entry.items.cold_furnace_ember.p0=A dark-red fleck in the black core has cooled, yet resembles the last shift's watchful eye.
lore.entry.items.cold_furnace_ember.p1=A hearth relic from the cold-altar cache, linking boiler and foundry history.
item.prosperity.cold_furnace_ember.name=Cold Furnace Ember
lore.relic.cold_furnace_ember=A dark-red fleck in the black core has cooled, yet resembles the last shift's watchful eye.
lore.entry.items.shelter_workbadge.title=Shelter Workbadge
lore.entry.items.shelter_workbadge.p0=The chipped badge names no occupation; in a crisis, recording a person's name may have mattered more.
lore.entry.items.shelter_workbadge.p1=The workers' shelter cache preserves it as a record of refuge and work.
item.prosperity.shelter_workbadge.name=Shelter Workbadge
lore.relic.shelter_workbadge=The chipped badge names no occupation; in a crisis, recording a person's name may have mattered more.
lore.entry.items.trench_medic_badge.title=Trench Medic Badge
lore.entry.items.trench_medic_badge.p0=A brass clasp sits on red fabric; mud cannot hide the holes left by repeated stitching.
lore.entry.items.trench_medic_badge.p1=A rescue token from the trench-infirmary cache.
item.prosperity.trench_medic_badge.name=Trench Medic Badge
lore.relic.trench_medic_badge=A brass clasp sits on red fabric; mud cannot hide the holes left by repeated stitching.
lore.entry.items.bridge_pass.title=Bridge Pass
lore.entry.items.bridge_pass.p0=Nail holes pierce the brass rim; it once let people cross, but could not keep the bridge from falling.
lore.entry.items.bridge_pass.p1=Earn it by defeating Mirror Guard, recording the end of its barracks watch.
item.prosperity.bridge_pass.name=Bridge Pass
lore.relic.bridge_pass=Nail holes pierce the brass rim; it once let people cross, but could not keep the bridge from falling.
lore.entry.items.webbed_shuttle.title=Webbed Shuttle
lore.entry.items.webbed_shuttle.p0=Dark fibers wrap the wooden shuttle; none is cleanly severed. Its mender seems to have wanted one more attempt.
lore.entry.items.webbed_shuttle.p1=Earn it by defeating Silent Weaver, recording the weaving mill.
item.prosperity.webbed_shuttle.name=Webbed Shuttle
lore.relic.webbed_shuttle=Dark fibers wrap the wooden shuttle; none is cleanly severed. Its mender seems to have wanted one more attempt.
lore.entry.items.cracked_sighting_lens.title=Cracked Sighting Lens
lore.entry.items.cracked_sighting_lens.p0=A crack divides its view; the observer still trusted one half to see someone return.
lore.entry.items.cracked_sighting_lens.p1=Earn it by defeating Riftstring Sniper, recording the watchtower line.
item.prosperity.cracked_sighting_lens.name=Cracked Sighting Lens
lore.relic.cracked_sighting_lens=A crack divides its view; the observer still trusted one half to see someone return.
lore.entry.items.resonant_clapper.title=Resonant Clapper
lore.entry.items.resonant_clapper.p0=A polished stripe crosses the curved brass; after the bell fell silent, its striking point still remembered sound.
lore.entry.items.resonant_clapper.p1=Earn it by defeating Resonant Bell, recording the bell station and its ritual clues.
item.prosperity.resonant_clapper.name=Resonant Clapper
lore.relic.resonant_clapper=A polished stripe crosses the curved brass; after the bell fell silent, its striking point still remembered sound.
lore.entry.items.foundry_heart_fragment.title=Foundry Heart Fragment
lore.entry.items.foundry_heart_fragment.p0=Firebrick embraces a brass heart; before the works stopped, many suppers depended on its remaining alight.
lore.entry.items.foundry_heart_fragment.p1=Earn it by defeating Rampart Breaker; the foundry achievement controls its restored account.
item.prosperity.foundry_heart_fragment.name=Foundry Heart Fragment
lore.relic.foundry_heart_fragment=Firebrick embraces a brass heart; before the works stopped, many suppers depended on its remaining alight.
lore.entry.items.hive_memory_knot.title=Hive Memory Knot
lore.entry.items.hive_memory_knot.p0=Root fibers and a grey cocoon form a knot; it may remember a district, rather than one person's dream.
lore.entry.items.hive_memory_knot.p1=Earn it by defeating Hive Mind; the sunken-factory achievement controls its restored account.
item.prosperity.hive_memory_knot.name=Hive Memory Knot
lore.relic.hive_memory_knot=Root fibers and a grey cocoon form a knot; it may remember a district, rather than one person's dream.
lore.entry.items.sky_ritual_foil.title=Sky Ritual Foil
lore.entry.items.sky_ritual_foil.p0=Only one angle joins the pierced foil's pattern, like a window the ground never possessed.
lore.entry.items.sky_ritual_foil.p1=Witness the timed court apparition at a cold altar, observatory or pilgrim arch. A site can reveal it daily; each player receives the witnessing token once.
item.prosperity.sky_ritual_foil.name=Sky Ritual Foil
lore.relic.sky_ritual_foil=Only one angle joins the pierced foil's pattern, like a window the ground never possessed.
lore.entry.items.mire_sounding_weight.title=Mire Sounding Weight
lore.entry.items.mire_sounding_weight.p0=Brass and cord retain bands of mud; the surveyor wanted to know whether the next step still had ground.
lore.entry.items.mire_sounding_weight.p1=An exploration token from the mire-grotto special cache.
item.prosperity.mire_sounding_weight.name=Mire Sounding Weight
lore.relic.mire_sounding_weight=Brass and cord retain bands of mud; the surveyor wanted to know whether the next step still had ground.
lore.entry.items.sealed_archive_tube.title=Sealed Archive Tube
lore.entry.items.sealed_archive_tube.p0=Brass hoops grip a dark wooden tube; the seal bears an unfinished date.
lore.entry.items.sealed_archive_tube.p1=A records token preserved in the city-archive special cache.
item.prosperity.sealed_archive_tube.name=Sealed Archive Tube
lore.relic.sealed_archive_tube=Brass hoops grip a dark wooden tube; the seal bears an unfinished date.
lore.entry.items.rail_repair_token.title=Rail Repair Token
lore.entry.items.rail_repair_token.p0=Tool outlines remain on an iron-grey tag, like a list left for the next repair shift.
lore.entry.items.rail_repair_token.p1=A repair token preserved in the rail-service special cache.
item.prosperity.rail_repair_token.name=Rail Repair Token
lore.relic.rail_repair_token=Tool outlines remain on an iron-grey tag, like a list left for the next repair shift.
lore.chapter.rise.title=The Cities Rise
lore.chapter.rise.p0=The first cities were no nobler than the wild. They gathered people willing to wait for each other around one furnace, and gave them a shared morning.
lore.chapter.rise.p1=Bridges crossed rivers, rails skirted forests and brass bell stations joined districts in time. Prosperity was written on machine plates and in the lamps of workers' shelters.
lore.chapter.rise.p2=The shelters, valve seats and relics have entries of their own. Walking through them brings you closer to old life than guessing from a complete map.
lore.chapter.collapse.title=The Day of Collapse
lore.chapter.collapse.p0=The disaster did not first knock at the court. It began in small things the cities trusted: pressure faltered, bells lost their agreement, and roads returned travelers to unfamiliar crossings.
lore.chapter.collapse.p1=People turned furnaces into ramparts and production lanes into shelters. They did try; the life they protected was simply larger than the walls.
lore.chapter.collapse.p2=Rampart Breaker and Hive Mind are echoes left after the disaster, not machines still running old production plans. Read their warnings and give both watches an ending that can be recorded.
lore.chapter.ember_roads.title=Roads Through Embers
lore.chapter.ember_roads.p0=After the furnaces cooled, shelter doors stayed open. Medics left cloth badges, repair crews left tool tags, and the switch keeper never reclaimed the heavy key.
lore.chapter.ember_roads.p1=Travelers can bring these objects back to the chronicle. They preserve records and clues; reading their accounts is not a reason to receive endless items.
lore.chapter.ember_roads.p2=Night echoes keep a different watch from ruin guardians. The former leave with daylight; the latter still belong to their rooms.
lore.chapter.five_watches.title=The Five Watches
lore.chapter.five_watches.p0=Boilers, looms, watchtowers, mirrored armor and bell stations once guarded parts of everyday life. After the disaster, their duties survive as forms that still answer a traveler.
lore.chapter.five_watches.p1=The five watches have distinct danger zones: spiral surges, binding fields, aim marks, frontal strikes and sound rings. Read their warnings first, then strike in the spaces between them.
lore.chapter.five_watches.p2=Actual defeats and achievement records restore this account's postscript. A borrowed token can tell its origin, but cannot stand in for a participant's record.
lore.chapter.five_watches.record=The five records now name not only their watchers, but those who understood them. The old city's time has moved one small step forward.
lore.chapter.foundry_subsidence.title=Foundry and Subsidence
lore.chapter.foundry_subsidence.p0=The foundry keeps its high loading bridge; the sunken factory keeps shafts to daylight. Both leave routes outward, as if workers last checked the exits for survivors.
lore.chapter.foundry_subsidence.p1=Rampart Breaker divides its court with quakes and fault lines; Hive Mind pulses and supports its production lanes. Their large silhouettes do not mean the same battle: they remember different final duties.
lore.chapter.foundry_subsidence.p2=The furnace-heart fragment and memory knot each come from a real defeat. Both achievements together restore the ending of this account.
lore.chapter.foundry_subsidence.record=Neither furnace heart nor hive chamber awaits another order. The works have not resumed, but their final shift can end.
lore.chapter.sky_court.title=The Distant Court
lore.chapter.sky_court.p0=Some sites left their prayers to the sky. The cold hearth, lens deck and pilgrim arch do not claim to rebuild an age; at night they offer the same distant vision to those who linger.
lore.chapter.sky_court.p1=The Celestial Court is a timed ritual apparition. It appears overhead and departs; no battle is required. Each site has a daily interval before it can reveal the vision again.
lore.chapter.sky_court.p2=The first witnessing leaves a ritual foil and personal record. Watching again revisits the vision without awarding another first-witness token.
lore.chapter.sky_court.record=The court above has departed; the foil remains in your hand. The rite rewrites no past, but reminds its witness that some farewells deserve to be seen to their end.
